# PsychoShare Network API - AI Context

## Project Overview

PsychoShare Network is a social network platform for psychologists to share Creative Commons licensed academic content, scientific articles, and educational materials. Features standard social media functionality with academic focus.

## Technical Stack

- **Backend**: .NET 8.0 with C#
- **Database**: MySQL 8.0+ with Entity Framework Core
- **ORM**: Entity Framework Core with Lazy Loading Proxies
- **Authentication**: JWT (JSON Web Tokens)
- **Architecture**: Clean Architecture with DAO Pattern
- **Testing**: xUnit (In Progress)
- **Dependency Injection**: Built-in .NET DI Container
- **Frontend**: Vanilla JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap (separate repo)
- **Admin Dashboard**: React (separate repo - in planning)

## Project Structure

```
PsychoShare-network-api/
├── psychoshare_api/          # Main API (Controllers, DTOs, Services)
├── entity_library/           # Domain entities (User, Post, Comment, etc.)
├── dao_library/              # Data access (Interfaces, EF implementations)
└── entity_library.Tests/     # Unit tests
```

## Core Features Implemented

- JWT authentication and authorization
- User management with profiles and avatars
- Post CRUD with pagination and search
- Comments system
- Likes functionality
- Following/follower relationships
- File uploads (Images, PDFs, Avatars)
- Admin features (Reports, Bans, Roles)
- Feed system with pagination

## Development Guidelines

### Code Standards

- **Language**: All code, comments, and commits in English
- **Naming**: PascalCase for classes/methods, camelCase for variables
- **Clean Code**: Self-documenting code, minimal comments
- **Architecture**: Clean Architecture, DAO Pattern, Dependency Injection
- **Validation**: Input validation on all endpoints
- **Error Handling**: Try-catch blocks with proper logging
- **DTOs**: Use DTOs for all API requests/responses

### Git Workflow

- **Main branches**: `main` (production), `development2` (development)
- **Feature branches**: Create from `development2`
- **Commits**: Clear, descriptive messages in English
- **No conventions enforced**: Team uses flexible branch naming

### Database Guidelines

- **Connection**: Environment variables via `.env.local`
- **Migrations**: Use EF Core migrations
- **Lazy Loading**: Enabled (use with caution for performance)
- **Relationships**: Properly defined with navigation properties

## AI Assistant Instructions

### When Suggesting Code

- Follow Clean Architecture and DAO pattern
- Use dependency injection (constructor injection)
- Create DTOs for request/response objects
- Include input validation
- Add error handling with logging
- Use async/await for database operations where beneficial
- Return proper HTTP status codes (200, 400, 404, 500, etc.)

### When Creating Controllers

- Inherit from `ControllerBase`
- Use `[ApiController]` and `[Route("api/[controller]")]` attributes
- Inject `DAOFactory` for data access
- Inject `ILogger<T>` for logging
- Use proper HTTP verbs (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- Return `IActionResult` with proper status codes

### When Creating Entities

- Place in appropriate folder (system/, social_media_core/, etc.)
- Define navigation properties for relationships
- Use proper data annotations if needed
- Consider lazy loading implications

### When Creating DAOs

- Define interface in `dao_library/interfaces/`
- Implement in `dao_library/entity_framework/`
- Inject `AppDbContext`
- Use EF Core LINQ queries
- Handle null cases appropriately

### What NOT to Do

- Don't hardcode connection strings
- Don't use Spanish in code/comments
- Don't create unnecessary comments (code should be self-explanatory)
- Don't skip validation
- Don't ignore error handling
- Don't use Singleton pattern (use DI instead)

### Testing Approach

- Use Swagger UI for manual testing
- Write xUnit tests for business logic
- Test via `http://localhost:5174/swagger`
- Verify all CRUD operations work correctly

## Current API Endpoints

### Auth & Users
- POST /api/user (register)
- GET /api/user/{id}
- PUT /api/user/edit/{id}
- GET /api/user/check-email

### Posts
- POST /api/post
- GET /api/post/{id}
- GET /api/post (paginated)
- GET /api/post/feed (with search)
- GET /api/post/user/{userId}
- PUT /api/post/{id}
- DELETE /api/post/{id}

### Social
- POST /api/comment
- GET /api/comment/post/{id}
- POST /api/like
- DELETE /api/like/{id}
- POST /api/following/follow
- DELETE /api/following/unfollow

### Media
- POST /api/image
- POST /api/pdf
- POST /api/avatar

### Admin
- POST /api/report
- GET /api/report
- POST /api/ban
- POST /api/role/assign

## Environment Setup

```env
DB_SERVER=localhost
DB_PORT=3306
DB_NAME=psychoshare
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_password
```

## Priority Focus Areas

- Maintain Clean Architecture
- Proper error handling and validation
